            <ArticleTitle>Diffuse large B-cell lymphoma presenting as piriformis syndrome.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>419-22</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1002/mus.21538</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Piriformis syndrome (PS) is a rare condition characterized by pain and paresthesia of the buttock, often radiating to the posterior thigh. A patient with sciatica that was clinically suspicious for PS, underwent diagnostic work-up. A diagnosis of diffuse large B-cell lymphoma with neurolymphomatosis (NL) was made. To our knowledge, this is the first report of NL presenting as PS. NL is a possible cause of secondary PS.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
